;; grog-odoo instances — ~/.config/grog/odoo-instances.edn
;;
;; Source of truth for the grog-odoo MCP server (GROG_ODOO_CONFIG env points at
;; this file; grog also rewrites it from grog.edn's legacy :odoo block once).
;; Credentials live HERE, in the config home — never in grog.edn / git.
;;
;; - `:name` is the only identifier the model may use. Selection is locked to
;;   these names; no tool accepts a URL/host/db from the model.
;; - With MORE THAN ONE instance configured, EVERY odoo_* call must name one
;;   with the `instance` argument. There is no default: a bare call is refused,
;;   so nothing can silently hit the wrong database.
;; - `:allow-write` (default FALSE) is the per-instance write switch. False
;;   means any statement that could modify data is refused before Odoo is even
;;   called. True passes mutating SQL to Select-O-Matic — which still requires
;;   the Odoo SUPERUSER account and an explicit confirmation.
;; - There is NO `:sql` block and no database connection any more: SQL goes
;;   through the `select_o_matic` addon over the Odoo API, using the instance's
;;   own login. No database host/port/credentials are needed.
{:instances
 [{:name "stage"
   :url "https://exclave.cmsaero.com"
   :db "odoo18_stage"
   :user "admin"
   :password "secret-or-api-key"
   :allow-write false}

  {:name "prod"
   :url "https://odoo.example.com"
   :db "odoo18"
   :user "admin"
   :password "..."
   :allow-write false}]}
